(LIB-19 through LIB-24 -- writing a library. The mathkit worked example,
 LANGUAGE.md:5460-5466, compiles with --shared to a self-contained .so
 exporting exactly its two functions, mangled, with zero relocations, plus
 a beside-it .lib naming an identity. Needs --shared and nm/readelf, so it
 is not auto-run by check-probes.sh; this file and its recorded output are
 the hand-verification record. LIB-20 is this same invocation. LIB-21 is
 the nm/readelf facts below -- exactly the library's own two functions
 exported, nothing else, zero relocations. LIB-22/LIB-23 restate those as
 the manual's own prose. LIB-24 is the Library declaration visible in the
 .lib output below, which LIB-noidentity.vox shows is mandatory.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox
   docs/ledger/probes/libraries/shared/LIB-writing.vox --shared -o libmathkit.so
 expected: exit 0, and:
   nm -D --defined-only libmathkit.so
     000000000000072c T mathkit_1_0_add_two_numbers
     000000000000076c T mathkit_1_0_greet
   readelf -r libmathkit.so
     There are no relocations in this file.
